   "notes": "Cockerell's Building (1837-42, now Caius Library), north front on Senate House Passage: warm sandstone ashlar, heavily rusticated base (~6 m) with small square windows, then deep-set tall rectangular windows between giant pilasters, round-arched upper windows under a heavy classical cornice. Bay count (11) estimated from oblique views down the passage."
